# Solidity / NatSpec

Application code elsewhere forbids comments. **Contracts are the exception.**

## Required

- NatSpec on public/external functions and events: `@notice`, `@param`, `@return` as applicable.
- `@title` / `@author` on contract if part of a deployable module.
- `@dev` only for non-obvious safety, invariants, or trust assumptions.

## Forbidden

- Inline noise (`// increase i`).
- Commented-out code.
- Duplicating what the signature already says.

## Quality

- Checks-effects-interactions; explicit visibility; custom errors over string reverts when targeting modern Solidity.
- No unbounded loops on user-controlled length without a hard cap.
